# Security

- Never commit `.env`, credentials, API keys, or connection strings with passwords.
- Never hardcode secrets in source.
- Validate input at the API. Authorize on the API.
- Hash passwords with a proven hasher when auth is implemented.
- Use EF Core parameterization; no string-concatenated SQL.
- CORS allowlists from configuration.
- Do not log tokens, OTPs, or passwords.
- Admin capabilities must not leak into public routes or sitemaps.
